aining the respective prowess of Visnu and the blue-throated one, asked the great-father, foremost of those abiding by truth, reading the intention of the deities, fomented a quarrel between them.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-10","DUTT-1-75-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2165c3d329ffbf4d55a327ba9ab914672953a2decf0261751b837f04697f081d","compact":"4ce35802b9ce75ee5fc241b70acb74736ef8c687bd04b4073f0f7496f89b4c0c","nasal":"4ce35802b9ce75ee5fc241b70acb74736ef8c687bd04b4073f0f7496f89b4c0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":14,"english":"O Kākutstha, equal in energy to the bow belonging to Rudra. Once on a time the deities, with the object of ascertaining the respective prowess of Visnu and the blue-throated one, asked the great-father, foremost of those abiding by truth, reading the intention of the deities, fomented a quarrel between them.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"825c3f86954d134d0ff3daeb4bcedf7975fbc57162c9c4ae27e5b370dc3a1e90","compact":"bd90a25960506962e0ee34f8b979d05e1839d79d55cebda1a7944f26c312f5aa","nasal":"f4404399eaa426975f5da8baa186a380aaf3d6d3966bffe323cfd99272add6a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":15,"english":"O Kākutstha, equal in energy to the bow belonging to Rudra. Once on a time the deities, with the object of ascertaining the respective prowess of Visnu and the blue-throated one, asked the great-father, foremost of those abiding by truth, reading the intention of the deities, fomented a quarrel between them.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6375aa3722457d9b375ecab7cce82cdd30e4a569a13154e80648b49c27d330bd","compact":"2dde8940ca4ff524ead504e6edeed07c50013a065a5d16d10d26393879a682d9","nasal":"2dde8940ca4ff524ead504e6edeed07c50013a065a5d16d10d26393879a682d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":16,"english":"O Kākutstha, equal in energy to the bow belonging to Rudra. Once on a time the deities, with the object of ascertaining the respective prowess of Visnu and the blue-throated one, asked the great-father, foremost of those abiding by truth, reading the intention of the deities, fomented a quarrel between them. Upon that quarrel breaking out among the deities, there took place a mighty contest capable of making one's hair stand on end, between Vişnu and the blue-throated one, each burning to beat the other down.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-11","DUTT-1-75-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5396d69336b111d056b99c3acdf2f2b58a9969c9abc4be5ecd07e51d92c06d63","compact":"e46b86d308f27e48e0f1345d83a461c669a54216049c286cb68fa815ff3ebfab","nasal":"12ac89486c6e53addb7a0c19c451364c11045378f7734294ea2b2557be7a2f79"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":17,"english":"Then on Vişņu uttering a roar, Siva's bow of dreadful prowess became flaccid. And thereupon the three-eyed Mahadeva became moveless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.903,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f0e941f6b6ef02a5b7c89e3c3974af0f769cdb53aecdc9d3456a1ed73423ba0","compact":"848f26459f19e295ff1485789184974e2c1f813bbdbdc540b05947b6200d9b50","nasal":"c4a85fbfd19b995a7fe16513b37e84ba32f764a77f301909b5ea75268016b522"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":18,"english":"Upon the assembled gods with the saints and the Cāraṇas beseeching those two foremost of celestials, they became pacified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26ac5643f3dbb10bd3366d0f1672e3bd45388ae47272ccba442a92513d1d0276","compact":"e3e153bbbc8df6b6d4fb929ca02669a66e3589a5bce9e1f7a2b75301979409e5","nasal":"e3e153bbbc8df6b6d4fb929ca02669a66e3589a5bce9e1f7a2b75301979409e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":19,"english":"Upon beholding that bow of Śiva rendered flaccid by Vişnu's prowess, the deities with the saints acknowledged Vişņu as the more powerful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.972,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c024d93b5eb06fe30a7cb22af5a9113de00ec2752cbe424438930bf856b0909","compact":"9ea38ac5938af32cdc9295241bbe29cff86e42d6355e22437cdbcc4246d6f29f","nasal":"a8b2883a84c6e18d64df608750ab4015865c495b96b5af4eab2a0c3690f09948"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":20,"english":"The enraged Rudra of high fame made over the bow along with its shafts to the hands of the Rajarsi, Devarata of Videha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b338c19bf2af521fbbfc0f663a41d45565674bf25bad4159076b25afc7b5975","compact":"f78e52f2c7e091bb6aaa8a9f809eefd4c85025f4fbc951c49d1264011b5e3362","nasal":"f78e52f2c7e091bb6aaa8a9f809eefd4c85025f4fbc951c49d1264011b5e3362"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":21,"english":"O Rāma, this bow belonging to Vişnu, capable of conquering hostile cities, Vişnu consigned to Bhrgus' son, Reika, as a worthy trust.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"57d66e1e3438f561398b97058ad9d6139d3f6a7afcde9ab578fd1226b21e13b9","compact":"d88e2834187ffce988c319e79095fb462ea9619e0e9db3464f03f9714c939021","nasal":"d88e2834187ffce988c319e79095fb462ea9619e0e9db3464f03f9714c939021"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":22,"english":"The exceedingly energetic Rcīka made over the divine bow to his son of immeasurable prowess, my sire the high-souled son of Jamadagni.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5fda2e494fa20f0be7bc717c298db91bda848569cd66be2161951422e0e9f4a3","compact":"c59a499ad0b525365886b86a0614a3b9aad5f8db330a2b26e79cee84dfed00f5","nasal":"c59a499ad0b525365886b86a0614a3b9aad5f8db330a2b26e79cee84dfed00f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-23","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":23,"english":"Once on a time, on my sire surcharged with ascetic energy, renouncing the bow, Arjuna, under the influence of unrighteous sentiment, compassed the death of my father.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074023","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"316aebacaabe586b688a19bad91f4a79ea6e8b5bedca53f0c2714436afa9674a","compact":"d31f4cbb4435415c18f88ba3a7068bda2b7ce025b6ffb1a704a8bf39e7148e2e","nasal":"d31f4cbb4435415c18f88ba3a7068bda2b7ce025b6ffb1a704a8bf39e7148e2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-24","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":24,"english":"Thereupon, learning of the lamentable and untoward slaughter of my sire, I from ire, annihilated the Kșatryas, springing up afresh by numbers, then bringing under sway the whole earth, I, O Rāma, on the sacrifice being over, conferred it upon the righteous Kasyapa as Daksina.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074024","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce31bb5f68df19ba86b83c5ae8c7456f7d2fbde020e9f29c74c221911d09c91d","compact":"d6f63e8111de353f4c2247937c78d00e20cafe646cff2b35547fa8bed1362514","nasal":"d6f63e8111de353f4c2247937c78d00e20cafe646cff2b35547fa8bed1362514"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-74-25","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":74,"verse":25,"english":"Thereupon, learning of the lamentable and untoward slaughter of my sire, I from ire, annihilated the Kșatryas, springing up afresh by numbers, then bringing under sway the whole earth, I, O Rāma, on the sacrifice being over, conferred it upon the righteous Kasyapa as Daksina.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.731,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-75-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1074025","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"033668a5b0f90beb3cc0c5054bffa6b2a